## What the licence covers

`LICENSE` is an MIT grant over **this project's own work**: the platform layer
under `platform/`, the port-only sources (`src/**/Port*.cpp`, `*PortStub.cpp`),
the build and packaging scripts, the tests, the tooling under `tools/`, and the
documentation under `docs/`. Those files carry no licence header of their own,
so this is where their terms are stated.

## What it does not cover

**The game code is not covered, and cannot be.** `src/` and `include/` are the
PrimeDecomp decompilation of *Metroid Prime 2: Echoes* (`G2ME01`, USA v1.00),
recompiled here for the host. That material derives from Nintendo's retail
executable, no permission to redistribute it is asserted here, and the MIT
grant above deliberately stops at this project's own code rather than sweeping
those directories in. Upstream PrimeDecomp's own dedication of its work is kept
as `LICENSE-decomp`; it speaks for the decompilation's authors, not for
Nintendo. Anyone who obtained this repository obtained a working copy; that is
a separate question from what may be redistributed, and it is one only the
copyright holder can answer.

**The console SDK and runtime are not covered either.** `extern/sdk/` holds the
decompiled Dolphin (GameCube) SDK, the Metrowerks C library headers and the
CodeWarrior runtime. Like `src/` and `include/`, they come from the retail
executable and its toolchain, belong to their owners, and are outside the MIT
grant. The same goes for the per-version symbol and split data under `config/`,
which describes that executable.

**No game assets may be packaged with a build.** Not the disc image, not the
executable or its REL modules, not extracted PAK/STRG data. The build takes no
game data at all; the port reads the user's own disc image at run time, and
`tools/make_appimage.sh` says so in its own help text. The only images the port
ships are its own icon (`packaging/varia-bolt.svg`) and controller-button
glyphs built from CC0 sources (`tools/prompt_icons/`).

